    "Description": "Migration slice 2 (docs/blueprints/ReverseToBaseline_Slice_Design.md): blueprint-authored rebuild of the C# oracle HillAttackTankNodes.Action_ReverseToBaseline (~line 456) -- an AiPrimitive BTreeAction. Graph: EventEntry -> ChannelCommand(LocomotionChannel/MoveTo) [explicit data-in pins Destination/Speed/ArrivalRadius/ReverseAllowed; Destination wired from a pure FunctionCall VectorOps.Vec3(GetParameter(BaselineX), GetParameter(BaselineY), Literal 0f); Speed/ArrivalRadius/ReverseAllowed baked via PinDefaults] -> WaitForChannel(LocomotionChannel) [AiPrimitive latent lowering: issues the command once, suspends: Running while channel Running, auto-Failure on channel Failure, continues to Out on channel Success] -> PublishEvent(ClearBehaviorEvent, Target pin left unwired => self-default, Entity=self) -> Return(Success). DEVIATION (documented, see design doc §2): the oracle publishes ClearBehaviorEvent on BOTH Success and Failure; WaitForChannel's lowering auto-returns Failure on channel failure WITHOUT running the post-wait chain, so this blueprint publishes ClearBehaviorEvent only on the Success path -- accepted simplification (no blueprint primitive injects a publish into the latent auto-failure path). New curated helper: Hrot.AI.Behaviors.Brains.VectorOps.Vec3/Vec2 (reflection-free Vector3 construction; no vector-literal node exists). Does not modify the C# oracle.",
